cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or these results, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Neuron Reflection: reflecting Qwen3-8B's neurons and attention heads to swap, fuse, remove or split a concept"
authors:
  - name: "@_a9lim"
    website: "https://a9l.im"
  - name: "@treetowntree"
    website: "https://logits.ml"
  - name: "Claude"
    website: "https://www.anthropic.com/claude"
abstract: >-
  Edits Qwen3-8B's MLP neurons and attention heads in place, without training, by reflecting (k = 2),
  projecting (k = 1) or amplifying (k < 0) their read and write vectors along a contrast axis taken from
  the neuron-lens lenses or from activations, or by mapping them through a linear map between sets of
  concepts. Related concepts collapse, unrelated ones dissolve, the AI persona can be refiled under
  another category, sets map onto sets with the model choosing the pairs, 30-100 neurons chosen by effect
  do what thousands chosen by loading do, projection fuses where reflection swaps, and a split holds only
  when the new kind borrows one the model already has. Every claim is measured against random-axis and
  random-unit controls, with its limits stated.
repository-code: "https://github.com/stdlogits/neuron-reflection"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - mechanistic interpretability
  - weight editing
  - neurons
  - attention heads
  - Householder reflection
  - Qwen3-8B
